      "stability-tests": "Only subsheaves of intermediate positive rank with torsion-free quotient are tested, as in Jacob Definition5.",
      "rank-one": "There are no intermediate-rank tests for a line bundle.",
      "theta-zero": "At theta=0 all subsheaves are preserved and the commutator term vanishes.",
      "indecomposability": "A holomorphic splitting into two nonzero bundles contradicts stability: the two smaller slopes cannot have the total slope as their weighted average.",
      "classic-existence": "Li--Yau existence for stable locally free bundles on compact Gauduchon manifolds is an explicit accepted classical input; no original full proof is certified.",
      "jacob-conversion": "Jacob degree divides by (n-1)! and volume by n!; their ratio gives the book factor n. Multiplying slopes by a common positive factor preserves stability.",
      "constant-sign": "Positive degree, rank and omega volume force the Einstein constant positive.",
      "complement-bound": "Positive mean gives one positive directional curvature eigenvalue, so the retained exhaustion gives n+r-1.",
      "product-factors": "Each factor separately has positive definite Einstein mean; no product stability is needed.",
      "product-vectors": "The retained tensor trace theorem covers every vector, including nondecomposable tensors.",
      "product-count": "There is one positive tangent eigenvalue per independent tangent block, giving n+r-k.",
      "flat-metric": "Fix the specified unitary flat Chern metric before choosing disc and sphere radii.",
      "compact-exception": "Compact K in the complement stays uniformly away from the removed zero section.",
      "parallel-frames": "Flat unitary Chern connections have parallel holomorphic unitary frames on simply connected patches.",
      "sphere-descent": "Constant unitary transitions preserve the sphere and its probability measure.",
      "average-smooth": "The sphere is compact and psi smooth, so derivatives commute with the local integral.",
      "horizontal-positivity": "The constant nonzero sphere vectors define holomorphic horizontal sections; their Hessians are strictly positive.",
      "maximum-contradiction": "A smooth function on a positive-dimensional compact complex manifold cannot have positive definite complex Hessian everywhere.",
      "hopf-parameters": "n>=2 and real q,a in (0,1); the deck action is free and properly discontinuous.",
      "metric-descent": "2b log(q)+2log(a)=0; the line metric descends.",
      "curvature-sign": "b<0, so the normalized curvature -b alpha is semipositive.",
      "curvature-rank": "Cauchy--Schwarz gives the radial kernel Cz and n-1 strictly positive directions.",
